where 𝜃, is the folding angle of an ideal crease, 𝑡 is the thickness of the material. When 𝜃,=0, 
===== PAGE 7 =====
 
the flat state, the hinge length ℎ,=𝑡, and when 𝜃,=±𝜋2, in the maximum folded state, the hinge length  ℎ,=2𝑡2. Finally, when 𝜃,=±𝜋, the stacked state, the hinge length ℎ,=𝑡. Dur-ing the entire folding range, we have 2𝑡2≤ℎ,≤𝑡. A simulation of the folded and stacked states of a cube model with different thicknesses can be found in Figure 1(e). 
