codex
The construction is sound on all tested sizes (including a doubled 506-panel build), but the generic cycle-cover DPLL is already showing the intended gap: tens of nodes at 126 panels, while the 254-panel shipping case is substantially harder. I’m letting the bounded reference run finish or hit its explicit cap; that result determines whether this remains an honest Track B family.
