codex
Outcome: **parked as `cap_bound`**, not rejected or shipped.

The Track B voxel-surface Hamiltonian-cycle generator is valid and all local gates pass. However, the oracle solved at least one instance at every writable preset; the next level requires 258 answer atoms, exceeding the 256-atom cap. This follows the paper’s Section B formulation and honestly discloses its efficient graph algorithms. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.03302)

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.03302/gen_1803_03302.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.03302/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.03302/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Harness metadata](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.03302/.meta.json)
- [README and cap-bound analysis](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1803.03302/README.md)

Key measurements: G1 passed 16/16, G4 found 0/200,000 guesses, all five G6 attacks scored 0/8, and the reference algorithm solved 8/8. No `REJECTED.md` or fabricated G9 transcripts were created; the special `cap_bound` rule requires stopping here.
